Tuesday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold XOM calls for gain. Adjust CAT calls. Buy SPWR calls* S=
tocks inch higher as fiscal stimulus package advancesStocks are inching hig=
her after starting the day in the red as Democrats made progress on Preside=
nt Joe Biden's $1.9 trillion economic relief program.The Dow Jones Industri=
al Average added less than 0.1% while the Standard &amp; Poor's 500 was off=
 by less than 0.1%. The Nasdaq rose 0.3%. Energy was the steepest decliner =
and communications the biggest gainer after midday on Tuesday.House Ways an=
d Means Chairman Richard Neal reportedly released Monday legislation in sup=
port of full stimulus payment to individuals earning $75,000 annually and c=
ouples earning $150,000 a year, in line with the criteria used to select pe=
ople who got the first two payments. This implies people who received the f=
irst two payments will be eligible for the proposed $1,400 stimulus checks,=
 bolstering optimism the Biden administration will force through the bulk o=
f the stimulus if bipartisan support from Republicans fails to materialize.=
Job openings rose to 6.65 million in December, according to the US Bureau o=
f Labor Statistics, above the 6.4 million openings expected in a survey com=
piled by Econoday and up from the 6.57 million openings reported in Novembe=
r. The December level represents 4.5% of total employment, up from 4.4% in =
November and 4.1% a year ago.In company news, shares of Hanesbrands (HBI) s=
urged by 23% intraday, the most on S&amp;P 500, after fiscal third-quarter =
sales beat forecasts and the low end of revenue and earnings guidance range=
 for the first quarter came in above market projections. The worst performe=
r on the index was Jack Henry &amp; Associates (JKHY), down 9% after fiscal=
 second-quarter sales missed estimates.Baidu (BIDU) advanced by 7%, the top=
 performer on Nasdaq, after the company said it rolled out its self-driving=
 mobility-as-a-service platform to power transportation services in Guangzh=
ou, China.Portfolio: Yesterday we sold our XOM and CAT calls at first targe=
ts for gains of 30% and 39%, respectively, which is great. Today we exited =
XOM for a profit on stop. ... Adjust target/stop for CAT. =E2=80=A6 We have=
 one new idea for you.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSExxon Mobil Corp. (XOM) Febru=
ary $45 calls-- Symbol: XOM210219C00045000-- Filled at $5.00 on Feb. 5. -- =
Sold half on Feb 8 at $6.50 for 30% gain!-- Sold second half today at 10:30=
 on stop at $5.40 for an 8% gain-- This trade is complete*Caterpillar (CAT)=
 February $190 calls-- Symbol: CAT210219C0019000-- Bought at $5.14 on Jan. =
5-- Sold half Jan 8 at $7.15 for 39% gain!-- Now trading at $9.00-- Set up =
to sell second half at new $9.45 &nbsp;lmt gtc-- Lift stop to new $8.00, go=
od after 10:30 a.m. ET only*NEW RECOMMENDATION SunPower Corp. (SPWR) Februa=
ry 48 calls-- Symbol: SPWR210219C00048000-- Order: Buy at $5.50 lmt day onl=
y-- If filled, set up to sell half at $6.90 lmt gtc and half at $8.90 lmt g=
tc-- If filled, set stop at $3.60 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks=
 for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expi=
ring on the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All=
 stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. A=
ll orders are good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orde=
rs expire at the close of the current session. Past results are no guarante=
e of future returns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. Recom=
mendations are leveraged and speculative, so only use risk capital =E2=80=
=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. All results are shown ex-commission=
s and fees. Options trading involves the risk of substantial loss. Some new=
s and research provided by Wall Street Journal, Bloomberg, Associated Press=
, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

